SLUG: services/storage-warehousing.html
TITLE: Storage & Warehousing in Kanpur for household goods
DESC: Short and long-term storage for household and office goods in Kanpur, inventoried in and out, charged by duration, with the rate confirmed in writing first.
HEADING: Storage &amp; warehousing
LEAD: For when the dates do not line up. Goods inventoried in, held for as long as you need, and delivered out when you are ready.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Services|/services.html ; Storage|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <h2>When storage is the sensible answer</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Possession dates rarely line up neatly. The gap between leaving one
            home and getting keys to the next is the most common reason people
            need storage — and planning for it is far cheaper than improvising.
          </p>
          <p>
            It also comes up when you are moving abroad for a fixed period,
            renovating, downsizing temporarily, or moving into a furnished
            place and needing somewhere for your own furniture to wait.
          </p>
          <p>
            Goods are inventoried as they go in, so you have a written record
            of exactly what is held, and inventoried again as they come out.
            Storage is billed separately from the move, by duration, and the
            rate is confirmed in writing before anything enters the facility.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-warehouse"/></svg></span>
          <h3>How goods are held</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Inventoried in and out, with a copy of the list for you</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Stored off the floor and wrapped, not stacked loose</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Short term, from a few days — or long term by the month</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Rate and billing period agreed in writing beforehand</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Delivered out on notice, when your new place is ready</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Worth knowing</span>
        <h2>Before you put things into storage</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Do not store food, liquids or batteries</h3>
          <p>
            Anything perishable, anything that can leak, and loose batteries
            should not go in. They are the usual cause of damage to everything
            stored around them.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Appliances must be fully dry</h3>
          <p>
            A washing machine or fridge with water still in it will develop
            mould in a closed space. Drain and dry both thoroughly before the
            move, not on the day.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Keep documents with you</h3>
          <p>
            Passports, deeds, certificates and anything you may suddenly need
            should never go into storage. Carry them yourself.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Decide early, not on the day</h3>
          <p>
            Storage arranged in advance is planned into the route and the
            inventory. Arranged on the day, it means a vehicle and crew
            waiting while space is found, and that is charged.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow">
        <h2>Questions we get asked</h2>
        <div class="faq mt-6" data-faq>
          <details>
            <summary>How is storage priced?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              By the volume held and the duration, separately from the move
              itself. You get the rate and the billing period in writing before
              anything goes in, so there is no open-ended charge running in the
              background.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I access my goods while they are stored?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              This is warehouse storage rather than a self-storage unit you
              hold a key to, so access is arranged on notice rather than on
              demand. If you expect to need regular access, tell us at
              booking — a self-storage unit may suit you better and we will
              say so.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is there a minimum period?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              There is usually a minimum billing period, which we confirm with
              your quote. Ask for it explicitly — a daily rate with a hidden
              monthly minimum is a common surprise in this industry.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are stored goods insured?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              Storage cover is separate from transit cover and is not automatic.
              Ask what is included, what it excludes and what the limit is, and
              get it in writing before goods go in.
            </p></div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-tight cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow text-centre">
        <h2>Need somewhere for your things to wait?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Tell us roughly how much and for how long, and we will quote the storage separately from the move.</p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-6 btn-row--centre">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact.html" data-open-callback>Request a callback</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/services.html">All services</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
